# Fantasy performance

- Prefer materialized caches over live `predict_*` on hub routes: `artifacts/draft_pool/`, `artifacts/weekly_predictions/`.
- Pool vs overlay: `build_draft_pool_payload()` then `build_value_overlay()` in `value_sheet.py`. Do not recompute the pool per request.
- Roster/cap reads are DB-only. Sleeper runs on link/sync, or `GET /api/hub/roster?live_sleeper=1` for a one-off pull.
- Scoring history lives in SQLite `sleeper_scoring_cache`. Refresh on league sync or `GET /api/hub/league/{id}/insights?refresh=1`.
- CPU-heavy work uses `app/process_pool.py`. Do not start a per-route process pool.
- Secrets and paths go through `src/config.py`, not raw `os.environ` in routes.
- `HUB_TIMING=true` logs slow hub routes (>500ms) and may set `X-Hub-Timing-MS`.
- After mlready or model changes, refresh the draft-pool fingerprint (`preseason_refresh` or `scripts/ops/fix_artifact_fingerprints.py`). Do not leave first-visit Fantasy pages on cold live inference.
